  "problem": "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c \\\\ d\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSuppose that $V=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}.$ Given that $B={{a}_{1},{a}_{2},b}$ is an orthogonal basis for $V,{a}_{1}\u22a5{a}_{2},$ and that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{a}{c}?$",
